{<b>Principle of Fast Arrival</b>

• In a game-forcing auction, jumping straight to game is the weakest auction by
either player.

• Delayed raise:

  1\S–2\H; 2NT–4\S

       3 spades, minimum values\n
       (13–15 support points)

       Possible hands:\n
       \SK Q 2  \HA Q 10 8 7  \D10 4  \CJ 4 2\n
       \SJ 5 4  \HA K 8 7 6  \DK 5 4  \CQ 2

  1\S–2\H; 2NT–3\S\n
       3 spades, extra values\n
       (16+ support points)

       Possible hands:\n
       \SK 4 2  \HA Q 8 7 6  \DA 2  \CK 3 2\n
       \SJ T 8  \HA K Q 8 7  \DQ 2  \CA Q 2

• Implied fit:

  1\S–2\H; 2NT–3\H vs. 4\H

• Opener can do, also:

  1\S–2\H; 3\H vs. 4\H\n
  1\H–2\D; 3\D vs. 5\D (rare)

• What about notrump?

  1\H–2\C; 2\D–2NT vs. 3NT

       More on this later}
[BCFlags "17"]
